ion to be lost.\\n\\nLet me examine the _coord_matrix function more closely to understand how it handles compound models.\\n\"}", "name": "think"}, "id": "toolu_12", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 225, "prompt_tokens": 13839, "total_tokens": 14064, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 13793, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 44}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "llm_metrics": {"accumulated_cost": 0.0, "max_budget_per_task": null, "accumulated_token_usage": {"model": "default", "prompt_tokens": 128923, "completion_tokens": 1604, "cache_read_tokens": 25875, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "context_window": 0, "per_turn_token": 14064, "response_id": ""}, "costs": [], "response_latencies": [], "token_usages": []}, "args": {"thought": "\nLooking at the _cstack function (lines 234-247), I can see a potential issue. When handling the '&' operator for compound models, the function:\n\n1. Computes the total number of outputs (noutp)\n2. For left model: calls _coord_matrix(left, 'left', noutp)\n3. For right model: calls _coord_matrix(right, 'right', noutp)\n4. For the else case on line 245: it sets cright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = 1\n\nThe problem appears to be in line 245. When the right operand is already a matrix (from a previous separability calculation), it's setting all values to 1 instead of preserving the existing matrix structure. This would cause the separability information to be lost.\n\nLet me examine the _coord_matrix function more closely to understand how it handles compound models.\n"}}
